{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Whoever lies with his father's wife.</b> Whether she is his mother or not. Whence his mother who is not his father's wife? Scripture says: לא תנאף. It is stated here regarding punishment: ערות אביו גלה, and it is stated further on regarding warning: ערות אביך לא תגלה. Just as in the warning Scripture made his mother who is not his father's wife like his mother who is his father's wife, as we expound: ערות אמך — to include his mother who is not his father's wife, so too here in the punishment Scripture made his mother who is not his father's wife like his mother who is his father's wife. And [regarding] ואיש כי יקח את אחותו, we exclude from it: ערות אחותך בת אביך או בת אמך and ערות בת אשת אביך, as we learned in chapter כיצד. <b>His father's wife</b> — this refers to his mother who is his father's wife." "<b>Et his father's wife.</b> It is stated here: ערות אביו גלה, and it is stated further on: ערות אשת אביך לא תגלה. Just as there it includes his father's wife after death, so too here it includes his father's wife after death — in chapter four of מיתות."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The citation לא תנאף (Exod. 20:13) is used as the prooftext for the prohibition with one's mother; the argument proceeds by gezeirah shavah between the warning and punishment passages.", 1 "The phrase בפרק ד׳ מיתות refers to the fourth chapter of Sanhedrin, which deals with the four modes of execution; the abbreviation ד׳ resolves as 'four.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:48.452540022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}